    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` (GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) computed on creation.\n\n**Level formula:** start at 1; +1 if an email is present; +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`; capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). The old GOLD/`householdSize` logic no longer feeds into it.\n\n## Files changed\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string-enum schema with a `membershipLevel` integer schema (`format: int32`, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `membershipLevel` and drops `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `@Mapping` now targets `membershipLevel`, and `membershipTier(...)` was replaced by a reusable `static int membershipLevel(Owner)` implementing the new formula.\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (via the shared `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`), per the spec's requirement that anything recording the tier record the level instead. Confirmed in the run: `AUDIT - Created owner id=11 ... membershipLevel=3`.\n\n4. **`AssignHouseholdId.java`** \u2014 removed the now-stale Javadoc reference to the \"GOLD membership tier\" (`householdSize` no longer drives membership).\n\n## Tests\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` case (unique name + email \u21d2 `membershipLevel` = 3) passes.\n\nOne note: `householdSize` is still persisted and set by `AssignHouseholdId`, but is now unused by the response mapping \u2014 I left it in place since removing a persisted column was out of scope for this change.",
